      "widgets_values": [
        "OmniCam -> MiniMax H3 Scene Coverage  (profile: h3_scene_coverage)\n\nWHAT'S DIFFERENT FROM h3_native / h3_api\nThis profile needs no playblast. It compiles the selected camera's own\norbit/arc directly into a complete H3 prompt plus H3EDIT_OPTIONS -- there\nis no reference video to record or resample.\n\nWHAT IT REPRESENTS\nOne continuous, target-centric camera orbit or arc around a fixed subject:\norbit left/right, elevation change, radius change, direction reversals, and\nexact loop closure when the camera returns to its opening view. A moving\ntarget, cuts, or a multi-turn path are BLOCKED at preflight with a\nrecommendation to use h3_native instead -- this example uses a plain 180 deg\norbit so it never depends on closure behavior.\n\nHOW TO USE\n1. Author a target-centric orbit in Director (no need to record a playblast).\n2. Queue once to compile. Read the preflight -- five checks specific to this\n   profile: h3_camera_representation, h3_camera_direction,\n   h3_camera_completion, h3_camera_timing, h3_loop_closure.\n3. Connect Monitor.final_prompt to TextEncodeH3Edit.compiled_prompt and\n   Monitor.h3edit_options to TextEncodeH3Edit.options. Wire the source image\n   straight to TextEncodeH3Edit.source_image -- OmniCam does not transport it.\n\nTIMING\nScene coverage resolves to 124, 243 or 362 frames at 24 fps, never shorter\nthan the authored move -- it stretches to the next supported length rather\nthan speeding the shot up."
      ],
